  "checks": [
    "InventoryGrid returns an independent copy of arranged viewport, content extent and offset. The copy survives grid and Context retirement.",
    "Absolute and relative changes, content-rectangle reveals, wheel input and slot reveals use the same update path. An unchanged offset retains the render cache. A changed offset updates painted ranges and hit testing.",
    "The native fixture rejects over-limit finite deltas and NaN with the previous offset intact. Boundary deltas clamp, growing viewport and content together preserves a valid offset, and empty grids reset the tested offset.",
    "The JIT, dynamic and static xlang fixtures exercise scrolling and retirement. The window example renders the initial grid in JIT and static AOT.",
    "The same matched packages pass 17 SVG observed-view checks on each platform, including checked failure before and after reload clears contents, alias invalidation, shared-module retirement and the public example."
  ],
  "costs": [
    "Generated calls target the native entry points directly. Reading a snapshot copies the fixed-size native record by value.",
    "Layout uses a temporary native scroll record so viewport and content-size updates publish together. Managed calls retain existing scope and checked status handling.",
    "The paired heap profile warms both paths, then alternates +8 and -8 pixels for 100 successful changes in each path on the same grid. It records XRT allocator operations and excludes drawing, construction and elapsed time."
  ],
